Bugfix: Preserve trailing spaces/dots in the last path component on Windows

On Windows, restic silently dropped trailing spaces and dots from the
last component of a path when resolving it to an absolute path, because
the underlying `GetFullPathNameW` API call strips them before restic
applies its `\\?\` long-path prefix. This meant that files or
directories with names like `dir-b ` or `file.` could be silently
renamed when accessed by restic (e.g. during backup or restore).

Restic now preserves a trailing run of spaces and/or dots on the final
path component when building the absolute, long-path-prefixed form of a
path, so such names are no longer altered.

https://github.com/restic/restic/issues/22059
